cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReMem in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "ReMem: outcome-aware adaptive memory for long-horizon AI agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kesarla
    given-names: Viswesh
    email: visweshkesarla@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/visweshdev/ReMem"
keywords:
  - llm agents
  - long-term memory
  - retrieval
  - credit assignment
abstract: >-
  A memory layer for AI agents that learns from task outcomes which memories help,
  supersedes replaced facts, retires useless ones without deleting them, and selects
  context under a token budget. Includes a controlled evaluation that reports its
  negative results (no measurable gain with a small real LLM, none on LongMemEval).
